--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATA NOTICES — the licence above covers the code in this repository only.

The bundled data in data/ comes from the following sources and keeps its own
licence and attribution requirements. Full provenance for every layer, including
the exact dataset URL and the published feature count, is written by the
pipeline into data/flood/index.json and data/manifest.json.

  Flood extents, hazard zoning, flow corridors, measured depths
      Greater Chennai Corporation and the National Remote Sensing Centre (NRSC),
      published via opencity.in — "Other (Public Domain)".

  Building footprints, roads, land use, place names, wetlands
      © OpenStreetMap contributors, licensed ODbL.
      https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

  Vector basemap tiles
      Protomaps basemap (derived from OpenStreetMap, ODbL).
      https://protomaps.com

  Ground elevation
      AWS Open Data — Terrain Tiles (Terrarium encoding), public domain.
      https://registry.opendata.aws/terrain-tiles/

  Rainfall
      Open-Meteo historical weather archive (ERA5 reanalysis), CC-BY 4.0.
      https://open-meteo.com

  Ward boundaries
      datameet Municipal Spatial Data, CC-BY.
      https://github.com/datameet/Municipal_Spatial_Data

  Fonts
      Noto Sans (Regular, Medium, Italic), SIL Open Font License 1.1,
      served as glyph sets via protomaps/basemaps-assets.

  Map rendering libraries
      MapLibre GL JS (BSD-3-Clause) and PMTiles (BSD-3-Clause), vendored in
      data/vendor/ so the app runs with no network access.

Attribution is displayed in the app footer at all times, as required by the
licences above. If you reuse this data, carry the attribution with it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODELLED VALUES — not published data.

The risk score, the modelled water depths, the rainfall threshold and the
wetland counterfactual are our own calculations on top of the published data
above. They are documented in README.md and in data/score/index.json and must
not be presented as government measurements.
